. ../../testutils.sh

# What the lowering checks of the runtime contract: a routine the runtime
# has must have a flat form of its port's registers, and a foreign function
# the runtime implements must agree with `base`'s declaration; and of the
# static objects it is given: one that holds another must hold one the
# program has. What does not stops the lowering, with the reason. It uses
# the code generator's modules, installed as the package `idris2-native`.
idris2 -p idris2-native -p idris2 Gen.idr -o gen > /dev/null
./build/exec/gen
